From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:03:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Show every SMC temperature

The 14-inch M4 MacBook Pro's SMC has 222 temperature keys, but its
device tree describes five of them, so hwmon shows five temperatures.

Turn on apple,discover-temperatures. The five described channels stay
temp1 to temp5 with their labels; every other readable 4-byte float
temperature key follows, labelled with its key.

The fan stays as it is: fan1 input, minimum, maximum and target are read
only, and the SMC runs its own fan curve, as under macOS. Manual control
remains behind the driver's unsafe fan_control parameter.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
index 0ad20390e7..791c38ebb0 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
@@ -172,6 +172,12 @@
 
 	smc_hwmon: hwmon {
 		compatible = "apple,smc-hwmon";
+		/*
+		 * Every other readable temperature key as well, labelled with
+		 * its key: 222 T keys on 1.612, of which the 4-byte floats
+		 * not described below become temp6 onwards.
+		 */
+		apple,discover-temperatures;
 
 		/*
 		 * On this machine TCMz read the same as the hottest P-core die
